{{Quote|What would you say you take home from playing Ahsoka?''"<br />"''That the journey isn't always easy, that it isn't always clear, that this isn't about magic, you know? To make things how you want them to be, it takes work and diligence and love to really make the difference. And I believe everybody has those powers, and everybody has to continue trying. It's not like you become a Jedi and then that's it, you're good. They have to keep making that choice.|An interviewer and Rosario Dawson|<ref name="Tells all">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2020/11/rosario-dawson-dave-filoni-mandalorian-ahsoka-tano-grogu|text=Star Wars The Mandalorian: Rosario Dawson Tells All About Ahsoka Tano|author=Anthony Breznican|date=2020-11-30|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20201207031817}}</ref>}}
'''Rosario Isabel Dawson''' is an [[Wikipedia:Actor|actress]] who portrays [[Ahsoka Tano]] in the [[Disney+]] live-action TV series, ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'' and ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]''.

==Biography==
===Early life===
Rosario Dawson started acting at the age of 15 and decided to pursue acting the next year. Her grandma had Dawson attend [[Wikipedia:Lee Strasberg Theatre and Film Institute|Lee Strasberg Theatre and Film Institute]] where she had the same class as future [[Anakin Skywalker]] actor [[Hayden Christensen]], and later co-starred with him in the film [[Wikipedia:Shattered Glass (film)|''Shattered Glass'']].<ref name="Tells all" /> She was a fan of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' and she watched it with her daughter.<ref name="Best of Jedi">{{SW|url=news/rosario-dawson-ahsoka-tano-interview|text=The Best of the Jedi: Rosario Dawson on Bringing Ahsoka Tano to Live-Action and ''The Mandalorian''}}</ref>

===''The Mandalorian''===
{{Quote|I remember when I put the contacts on, that was when it really solidified &mdash; the headpiece, the tails, the shape, the coloring, everything. Doing the face marking, doing my skin, wearing the costume, all of that was absolutely incredible. But I still kind of felt like I was in cosplay. The second the contacts went in, it was Ahsoka. I felt like I disappeared.|Rosario Dawson|<ref name="Tells all" />}}
In [[February]], [[2017]], a ''[[Star Wars]]'' fan asked Dawson on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] if she would ever play [[Ahsoka Tano]], and she replied that she would want to play the character. This caused ''Star Wars'' fans to be excited about Tano appearing in live-action. According to Dawson, someone at [[Lucasfilm]] forwarded the Tweet to ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' executive producer [[Dave Filoni]],<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> and he thought she would make a good Tano.<ref name="Tells all" /> Filoni and ''Star Wars'' then followed Dawson on Twitter, but nothing happened for a long time.<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> Filoni kept loosely aware of Dawson's [[Wikipedia:Marvel Cinematic Universe|Marvel]] career and he watched interviews of her expressing excitement for the role. Filoni later told<ref name="Tells all" /> executive producer<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> [[Jon Favreau]] that he wanted Dawson to play Tano.<ref name="Tells all" /> When Dawson and Filoni discussed the show, he revisited Dawson's casting and realized Dawson's age would fit Tano's age in the show, and he decided the casting would work. Filoni and Favreau did not want to include Tano in [[The Mandalorian Season One|Season One]].<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> Near the release of the first season, Dawson got a [[Wikipedia:FaceTime|FaceTime]] call from Filoni and Favreau, and they showed her visuals and concept from their plans for [[The Mandalorian Season Two|Season Two]]. They also showed art of Dawson as Tano, but Dawson had to go to audio due to poor reception. Filoni and Favreau then asked Dawson if she wanted to play Tano and she agreed.<ref name="Tells all" />

After being cast as Tano for the episode [[Chapter 13: The Jedi]], Dawson watched ''The Clone Wars'', ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', and the [[Star Wars saga|''Star Wars'' saga]] as preparation. She enjoyed seeing how Tano's physicality and voice changed as she evolved.<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> Dawson studied [[Ashley Eckstein]]'s portrayal of Tano in animation and tried her best to honor it. Many screen tests were done because the Volume tends to look magenta.<ref name="Tells all" /> Dawson played Tano like a wandering [[Wikipedia:Samurai|samurai]] and a knowledgeable [[Wikipedia:Knight|knight]]. Filoni pointed to [[Wikipedia:Gandalf|Gandalf]] from [[Wikipedia:The Lord of the Rings (film series)|''The Lord of the Rings'']] as a touchpoint, with all of this factoring into Dawson's portrayal of the character. Dawson wanted to have Tano's playfulness and fun, including her cocky eyebrow. She liked Tano's wisdom and how she is grounded after everything she has gone through. Dawson enjoyed having homages to the different aspects of Tano that she loved. One of her most memorable moments was when she first tried on Tano's costume. Dawson wanted to be as authentic to the animated Tano as possible, and she insisted on wearing blue contacts to match the character's eye color.<ref name="Best of Jedi" />

[[File:The_Mandalorian_Season_2_Ahsoka_Tano_Poster.jpg|thumb|left|140px|Ahsoka Tano character poster for ''The Mandalorian'']]
All of the prosthetics were built to Dawson's skull and body, and Tano's headband clipped in the back and held the [[lekku|headtails]] in place.<ref name="Tells all" /> The make-up artists tucked Dawson's hair away so she could wear the headpiece.<ref name="Ahsoka for life">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2022/05/rosario-dawson-ahsoka-tano-star-wars-series|text=''Star Wars'': Rosario Dawson Aims To Play Ahsoka Tano For Life|author=Anthony Breznican|date=2022-05-20|work=[[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']]|archivedate=20220520134642}}</ref> The total transformation initially took three hours.<ref name="EW Rosario Natasha">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@entertainmentweekly|name=Entertainment Weekly|link=Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|video=SNhSdfQI7Gc|text=Rosario Dawson and Natasha Liu Bordizzo on 'Ahsoka' &#124; Star Wars Celebration &#124; Entertainment Weekly|archivedate=20220723224705}}</ref> Dawson noticed that the horns and headtails were shorter than in the animated shows, but Filoni assured the actress it was necessary for stunts.<ref name="Ahsoka for life" /> Dawson thought the face markings, different skin color, and costume were incredible, but she did not feel like Tano until she put the contacts in.<ref name="Tells all" /> Dawson loved being able to provide new information about [[Din Grogu|the Child]] and being a storytelling device for new fans.<ref name="Best of Jedi" /> Dawson met<ref name="Tells all" /> ''Star Wars'' creator<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> [[George Lucas]] when he visited ''The Mandalorian'' set.<ref name="Tells all" /> Before the release of ''The Jedi'', Dawson was anxious about her performance and its reception.<ref name="Best of Jedi" />

===''The Book of Boba Fett''===
Dawson played Tano in "[[Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger]]," the sixth episode of ''The Book of Boba Fett.''<ref name="Chapter 6">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref> She did not learn that her character would interact with [[Luke Skywalker]] until the day of filming. She was very excited that she got to work with [[Mark Hamill]],<ref name="Rosario Dawson Tweet">{{Twitter|rosariodawson|status/1507180811782549504|Rosario Dawson|quote=Are you kidding?! I was freaking out. I'm still pinching myself that I got to work with MARK HAMILL as AHSOKA. I didn't know my scene was with LUKE till day of&hellip;! @bobafett|archivedate=20220325171648}}</ref> who provided Skywalker's voice in the episode.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

===''Ahsoka'' television series===
{{Quote|Man, I am not a workout-y person, and I'm in my 40s getting into the most physically demanding role of my life. [Ahsoka's] not someone who gets tired. I can't play this like a human. She is an ''indefatigable'' alien. She's precise. She's master-level. The challenge is for me to show up and express that. It's like, I won't necessarily work out for myself, but I'll work out for Ahsoka any day of the week. I'm a huge fan, and I don't want to watch and be like, 'Yo, Ahsoka's hand seems a little shaky there.'|Rosario Dawson|<ref name="Ahsoka for life" />}}
Dawson continued to play Ahsoka Tano in the ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'' television series.<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}}</ref> ''Ahsoka'' started production on [[May 9]], [[2022]],<ref name="Ahsoka begins">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-begins-production|text=''Ahsoka'', the Upcoming Disney+ Original Series, Begins Production}}</ref> which Dawson thought was the best birthday present. Dawson rewatched the animated shows as preparation for reprising her role.<ref name="Rosario Natasha SWCA">{{SWYouTube|8RZiIf_oEAc|Rosario Dawson and Natasha Liu Bordizzo takes the stage at SWCA 2022 &#124; Star Wars Celebration Live!}}</ref> She was grateful to be part of a franchise she can participate in as she ages. She cut most of her hair, leaving enough to be hidden comfortably under her headpiece.<ref name="Ahsoka for life" /> The makeup process had been reduced to an hour and a half while the total transformation would take about two hours, so it started at 4:30 or 5:00 in the morning.<ref name="EW Rosario Natasha" />

Dawson wanted to show how Tano does not get tired, so she dedicated herself to intense [[lightsaber]] and fight training as well as studying Tano's past.<ref name="Ahsoka for life" /> Dawson and [[Natasha Liu Bordizzo]], the actress who played [[Sabine Wren]], received [[Wikipedia:Chinese martial arts|wushu]] training from stunt coordinator [[Ming Qiu]]. Dawson showed Qiu freeze frames and clips from animated shows and asked Qiu to train her to do Tano's stunts. Qiu would say the stunts are not possible, but she showed Dawson what she could do instead.<ref name="Rosario Natasha SWCA" /> Dawson said that playing Tano in the show was the most physically demanding role of her life.<ref name="Ahsoka for life" /> She tried to show that Tano is struggling with balancing her humanity, experiences, and desires.<ref name="EW Rosario Natasha" />

At Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase at [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|Celebration Anaheim]],<ref name="20 Highlights">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-20-highlights-from-lucasfilms-studio-showcase|text=SWCA 2022: 20 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> Dawson was absent due to filming ''Ahsoka'',<ref name="Sneek Peek Footage">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/ahsoka-star-wars-celebration-rosario-dawson-natasha-liu-bordizzo-1235278204|text='Ahsoka' Stars Rosario Dawson, Natasha Liu Bordizzo Debut Sneak Peek Footage at Star Wars Celebration|author=Adam B. Vary;Angelique Jackson; Wilson Chapman|date=2022-05-28|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20220528200940}}</ref> so Filoni and Favreau played a video message from her in full costume from the show's set.<ref name="20 Highlights" /> Right after ''Ahsoka'' finished its third week of filming,<ref name="Sneek Peek Footage" /> Dawson attended the Mando+ panel<ref name="MandoPlus">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-mando-plus-panel|text=SWCA 2022: Sabine Wren Joins the Cast of ''Ahsoka'' and 6 Other Favorite Moments from the Mando+ Panel}}</ref> where she introduced the droid [[C1-10P|Chopper]] and showed a clip of her in full costume and glimpses of [[Hera Syndulla]] and Sabine Wren.<ref name="Sneek Peek Footage" /> It was then announced that Bordizzo would play Wren in the show.<ref name="MandoPlus" /> Dawson has said that she will be committed to her character until her story is fully told.<ref name="Ahsoka for life" />

